     1	# guard-measured-fit — the measured-fit leg (recreation + practice)
     2	
     3	_Built 2026-11-15 on HQ's charge (owed checks, 2026-11-15 ~08:02 EST), from the candidate spec filed in recreation Cycle-007 Wave-5's Condense and applied ad hoc since. This file is the leg's standing definition; before this build the leg existed only as candidacy text inside RUN records (Waves 5–6) and as a builder-side instrument — never as a guard with a call point. It owns ONE defect class: readability failures whose mechanism is **fit asserted, not measured** (readability stuck/under-floor in Waves 2, 3, 4, 5 and again in Wave 10 — T54 density, T57 attribution typography). It does NOT own timing anchors, density judgment, or any content-level failure; those classes stay with their own guards._
     4	
     5	## What the leg checks (per item, on the final recreation.html)
     6	For EVERY text element that carries subject content (titles, labels, captions-in-scene, cards, marquees, counters):
     7	1. **A measurement row exists, with provenance.** The item's build record contains a fit table with one row per subject text element: element id · container (box/strip/line) · the INSTRUMENT (harness run or rendered-measurement tool that produced the row) · the fitted element + stage geometry · MEASURED ink bounds after fitting (glyph ink height and width, from post-fit measurement of the rendered geometry at the 360 px stage) · container bounds · margin on the binding side. A text element with no row, or a row missing its measurement provenance, is a HIT. *(Provenance form added 2026-11-18, recreation Cycle 035 Condense — Amendment A12's paired landing: T196 + T197's model rows.)*
     8	2. **Fit is measured, never formula-claimed.** A row whose bounds are derived from the fitting formula's own assertion (font size × assumed factor — a character-width × factor MODEL) rather than from a post-fit measurement of the rendered geometry is a HIT — the formula is the claim, not the evidence (founding instances: T20's glyph-height overstatement, ink at 76% of claimed cell pitch; T19's floored 11 px phrase in a box that could not hold it; T57's attribution lines). In a seat with no browser binary, the lawful measurements are (i) harness post-fit ink measurement of the built spans, or (ii) rendered measurement with a NAMED stand-in font, the row labeled PROXY with the font named (demonstrations: T195 harness post-fit · T190 PIL rendered measurement, Cycle 035).
     9	3. **Legibility floor.** Measured subject-text ink height below ~11 px at the 360 px stage width is a HIT, whatever the formula claimed.
    10	4. **Hierarchy is measured too.** Where the design claims an intensity/size hierarchy between neighbouring text elements, the rows must show the measured ratio; a hue-only hierarchy against near-equal measured sizes is a HIT (T20's neighbour-window failure).
    11	
    12	## Output form (filed per item, pre-wave)
    13	`fit-table.md` in the item's artifact directory: the full row set (each row carrying its instrument/provenance per check 1; stand-in rows labeled PROXY with the font named) + a HIT list (empty = PASS for this leg). The wave's RUN cites the table's path + hit count per item. The leg's verdict is ADVISORY (owner's 2026-11-14 ruling): hits are priced into the build before scoring where the builder can cure them; hits carried into the scoring wave are printed in the RUN with their disposition. What is NOT advisory is the firing: a wave whose record lacks the fit table for any item prints INCOMPLETE.
    14	
    15	## Call point
    16	Pre-wave, per item, after the build and BEFORE the five-lens scoring wave (wired into recreation INSTRUCTION Amendment A6 and practice INSTRUCTION Amendment A-C008 — the legs run before scoring, not after). Practice re-attempts fire the same leg on the new attempt's file.
    17	
    18	## Scope honesty
    19	This leg proves text fits its container at phone width, measured. It does not prove the text is the right text, the right density, or readable in motion — timing, density judgment, and content stay with the scoring wave and their own guards.
    20	
    21	## Firing record
    22	- 2026-11-15: BUILT (this file). First firing owed: the next recreation wave + the next practice wave, unconditionally.
